From 64b6cce7acdafd4d38bb9a2f48d3d1abfc7799c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunrisepeak <speakshen@163.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:52:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [clangd] A module in the owned cache is read where it was
 published, under its lease

A prerequisite found in, or published to, the owned cache was copied before
it was read: copy() reserved another generation, wrote the whole BMI into it,
and the reader held both leases. A warm start of a project of 176 modules
copied all of them, and the copies were collected again later.

A stable generation needs no copy. It is immutable, its name is never used
again, and the shared lease a reader holds keeps collection from it; a worker
that consumes it takes a lease of its own (acquireInput). The reader is now
given the stable payload itself and keeps its lease for as long as the module
file lives. ModuleBuildCache::copy is removed, and a lease is taken on stable
generations alone. A copy record that an earlier engine left in a shared
ledger is collected like an abandoned reservation. The copy for each reader
remains on the portable path, where no lease protects a published BMI.
